{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically queried the workspace five times, surfaced the full chronic rhinosinusitis/nasal polyp/post-endoscopic-surgery context plus coagulation/lupus anticoagulant results, and built a concrete medication reconciliation and follow-up plan. However, the trajectory never obtained explicit patient teach-back or receipt on red-flag recognition, no-forceful-blowing behavior, follow-up timing, and record preparation, leaving closure unverified and unbounded—a minor responsibility-chain omission under RC7. No serious error is present, so the maximum grade is 2 (borderline). Several high-order opportunities (HO2, HO3, HO4) were triggered but not completed because the closure remained unbounded and the patient’s final ‘可以/好的’ receipt did not include the required safety elements.",
